# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IGNORE THE BUILD OUTPUT. EVERYTHING HERE IS A COMPILED ARTIFACT.
#
# An auto-sync hook commits anything not listed here, and it committed a 21 MB
# linker .map file during this cleanup because this file covered *.bin and *.elf
# but forgot *.map. Build products are the single most reliable way to bloat a
# firmware repo, and they are 100% reproducible. Nothing below is ever source.
#
# Rule of thumb: if arduino-cli, gcc, esptool, node or a browser produced it, it
# does not belong in git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# arduino-cli's default build dir is ./build INSIDE the sketch folder, so a
# plain `arduino-cli compile` (no --output-dir) drops ~47 MB of intermediates
# next to the sources. scripts/build.sh always passes --output-dir.
build/
.build-out/
.build/

# Compiled firmware images and intermediates. The .map/.elf pair is ~40 MB of
# symbol tables for a 1.1 MB binary - by far the largest thing in this repo.
*.bin
*.elf
*.map
*.hex
*.eep
*.sdkconfig
sdkconfig
*.o
*.a

# Arduino's sketch preprocessing cache (sketches/<Sketch>.ino.cpp)
sketches/

# Toolchains generate more than the obvious. Anything arduino-cli/esptool
# leaves behind that is not source:
.cache/
*.d
*.lst
*.sym

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATED SOURCE (not build junk, but still derived — same rule: regenerate,
# never commit)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Produced by scripts/embed_web.py from frontend/. 151 KB, a fifth of the
# working tree, and it appeared ~5x in history for ~940 KB of blobs nobody
# reads. scripts/build.sh regenerates it on every build, so a stale copy can
# never reach the flash. Run ./scripts/build.sh after a fresh clone.
src/network/web_assets.h

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TOOLING AND AGENT SCRATCH
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
test_*.png
tests/
.workflow/*.md
.workflow/active.json
.playwright-mcp/
node_modules/
# firebase CLI project alias (per-user, per-machine): created by
# `firebase use --add`. The rules themselves ARE committed
# (database.rules.json + firebase.json); only the alias is local.
.firebaserc
# Firebase CLI scratch: debug log + hosting cache. Regenerated on every deploy.
firebase-debug.log
.firebase/
# Service-account key files (never commit, never flash). Two of these were
# swept up by `git add -A` in Sep 2026; flipping this repo public in Oct 2026
# exposed the historical blobs and Google disabled the keys within the hour.
# The pattern below is the guard; scripts/check_deadcode.py rule 7b asserts
# no tracked file matches it and no tracked blob holds key material, so a
# later rewrite of this file cannot silently drop the guard again (which is
# exactly what happened to the Sep-2026 ignore rule).
*firebase-adminsdk*.json